  ('6caf59ce-d82e-581b-aaeb-8615cbbf936f', '38bf5630-62ec-54d4-af2b-f9b4c804b5f3', 15, 'Drawing a Home', 'In which Ilse tries to redraw Pell''s house from memory. The walls appear, empty and cold, and Pell asks her to scrape them away again.

Ash fell over Cindermere the way snow falls elsewhere, soft and constant, settling in the gutters and on the brims of hats.

