insert into public.story_tags (story_id, tag_id) select 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', id from public.tags where slug in ('space-station', 'first-contact', 'slow-burn-mystery') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('8cb7f90b-8bc3-542d-a9ee-6a9b8e3bfd63', 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', 1, '03:12', 'The message arrived at 03:12 station time, which was not unusual. Kestrel ran on a skeleton crew at night, and the relays never slept.

What was unusual was the timestamp. Ama Boateng read it twice, then checked the station clock against the beacon at Halden Colony, then read it again.

The message had been sent at 03:12, three days from now.

It was short. It was in her own call sign. And it said, in the clipped shorthand she had used every day for four years: KESTREL DARK. HULL BREACH RING C. DO NOT OPEN BAY SIX.

Kestrel turned slowly against the stars, and the long windows of Ring C swept through a field of distant, unblinking light.

"If it''s a prank, it''s a very good one. If it''s not, I''d rather not find out the hard way," Jonah said.

At 03:12 the next night, the relay chimed again.', 'published', now() - interval '5.871 days', now() - interval '5.871 days'),
  ('da6bc952-3e2a-5947-a74b-6b7c5a08773d', 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', 2, 'Checking the Clocks', 'In which Ama verifies every time source on the station. All agree with each other, and the message still claims to come from later.

Out past the station, the relay dishes tracked their distant targets with the patience of things built never to blink.

Ama found herself counting hours the way some people counted breaths.

"If it''s a prank, it''s a very good one." Jonah paused. "If it''s not, I''d rather not find out the hard way."

The comms room hummed with relay traffic, a thousand voices from a dozen colonies passing through on their way somewhere else.

The future, it turned out, had her handwriting. That bothered her more than anything else.

The new message was longer this time. It ended with a name she did not recognise.', 'published', now() - interval '5.577 days', now() - interval '5.577 days'),
  ('8b7b70a2-e872-5363-ab84-6589c51a6b1c', 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', 3, 'Telling Jonah', 'In which Ama confides in engineer Jonah Ferris. He laughs, then quietly runs a structural scan of Ring C that night anyway.

Kestrel turned slowly against the stars, and the long windows of Ring C swept through a field of distant, unblinking light.

If she warned them and nothing happened, she was a fool. If she didn''t and something did, she was worse.

"You know what''s worse than a message from the future? One that knows your coffee order," Jonah said.

The galley smelled of reheated noodles and coffee that had been on the warmer since last shift.

Ama found herself counting hours the way some people counted breaths.

"If it''s a prank, it''s a very good one. If it''s not, I''d rather not find out the hard way," Jonah said.

Down in Ring C, the hull groaned like something stretching after a long sleep.', 'published', now() - interval '5.376 days', now() - interval '5.376 days'),
  ('c61d3980-d42e-5d60-a13b-8e16391ed16b', 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', 4, 'Bay Six', 'In which Bay Six is listed as an empty storage bay. Its access log shows it was opened eight months ago by an account that does not exist.

Out past the station, the relay dishes tracked their distant targets with the patience of things built never to blink.

Ama had spent four years listening to other people''s messages. She had never expected one to be addressed to her.

Commander Reyes said, "I need facts, Boateng. Not ghosts in the relay buffer."

The comms room hummed with relay traffic, a thousand voices from a dozen colonies passing through on their way somewhere else.

If she warned them and nothing happened, she was a fool. If she didn''t and something did, she was worse.

"You know what''s worse than a message from the future?" Jonah paused. "One that knows your coffee order."

The new message was longer this time. It ended with a name she did not recognise.', 'published', now() - interval '5.268 days', now() - interval '5.268 days'),
  ('bfec31b7-93f0-5569-ac05-cb7ceffafecf', 'a3c50a76-8cd6-561e-a2bc-56f43dace8ae', 5, 'Commander Reyes', 'In which Ama reports to Commander Reyes, who orders the messages logged as a relay fault and Bay Six left sealed.

Kestrel turned slowly against the stars, and the long windows of Ring C swept through a field of distant, unblinking light.

Every log she checked made the station look more ordinary, and the messages more impossible.

