insert into public.story_tags (story_id, tag_id) select 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', id from public.tags where slug in ('cultivation', 'sect-politics', 'revenge') on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('488936a0-9684-5f99-a660-79be77160b9e', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 1, 'Servants'' Gate', 'The servants'' gate of the Azure Summit Sect was a narrow stone arch, worn smooth by ten thousand bowed heads. Wei Lan bowed hers as low as the rest.

She had practised it in the mirror of a ruined well for three months. The bow of someone who had never been anyone. The posture of someone grateful for rice.

In the sleeve of her plain grey robe, wrapped in a strip of her mother''s mourning cloth, a cracked jade slip pressed against her wrist. It was cold. It was always cold. Her grandfather had died to keep it from these mountains, and she had just carried it through their front door.

Mist clung to the nine peaks of the Azure Summit, and the bells of the inner sect drifted down through it like falling leaves.

"The Dao does not care how much you hate." Elder Mo paused. "It cares how long you can sit still."

On the highest peak, a bell rang that had not rung in a hundred years.', 'published', now() - interval '97.706 days', now() - interval '97.706 days'),
  ('f736fa70-fe0a-5612-a432-e008252c1cf5', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 2, 'Crippled Meridians', 'In which a sect physician declares her meridians too damaged to cultivate. That night, following the slip, she draws in her first thread of qi.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

The jade slip grew a little warmer each time she followed its method. She chose not to wonder why.

"The Dao does not care how much you hate. It cares how long you can sit still," Elder Mo said.

In the servants'' quarter, the kitchen fires smoked and the floor was always damp no matter how often it was swept.

Her meridians ached as if packed with sand, and still the qi crept through them, slow and stubborn as a root through rock.

When she returned to her mat, someone had searched her belongings and left everything exactly in place, except one thing.', 'published', now() - interval '95.474 days', now() - interval '95.474 days'),
  ('453fa945-7ea5-5fe6-ad5c-c745ccd80a15', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 3, 'The Scripture Pavilion', 'In which assigned to dust the Scripture Pavilion, Wei Lan finds old sect records that skip one particular year entirely: the year her family died.

Mist clung to the nine peaks of the Azure Summit, and the bells of the inner sect drifted down through it like falling leaves.

She reminded herself that a servant who looks up is noticed, and a servant who is noticed does not survive.

"Revenge is a fire." Elder Mo paused. "Keep it small enough to warm your hands, not large enough to burn your house."

Pine resin and incense hung in the air of the Scripture Pavilion, along with the dust of a thousand unread scrolls.

The jade slip grew a little warmer each time she followed its method. She chose not to wonder why.

"The Dao does not care how much you hate." Elder Mo paused. "It cares how long you can sit still."

By morning, word had spread through the servants'' quarter: an elder was asking about the new girl.', 'published', now() - interval '93.071 days', now() - interval '93.071 days'),
  ('6406fea0-1539-5772-a59d-063a20181abd', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 4, 'Elder Mo', 'In which The pavilion''s keeper, the sleepy Elder Mo, catches her reading restricted records. Instead of punishing her, he asks what she is looking for.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

Wei Lan counted her breaths the way her grandfather had taught her: nine in, nine held, nine out.

"You sweep like someone who has never swept before. Who are you really, servant Wei?" Shen Rui said.

In the servants'' quarter, the kitchen fires smoked and the floor was always damp no matter how often it was swept.

She reminded herself that a servant who looks up is noticed, and a servant who is noticed does not survive.

On the highest peak, a bell rang that had not rung in a hundred years.', 'published', now() - interval '90.536 days', now() - interval '90.536 days'),
  ('c5e0fdfa-e160-57fe-a482-f34c249dd7f5', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 5, 'Shen Rui', 'In which inner disciple Shen Rui humiliates a servant in the courtyard. Wei Lan intervenes with a single, precise push that leaves him staring at her.

Mist clung to the nine peaks of the Azure Summit, and the bells of the inner sect drifted down through it like falling leaves.

Every face in the inner sect might have been there that night. She had to learn which ones.

"In this sect, the ones who bow lowest often climb highest." Shen Rui paused. "Remember that."

Pine resin and incense hung in the air of the Scripture Pavilion, along with the dust of a thousand unread scrolls.

Wei Lan counted her breaths the way her grandfather had taught her: nine in, nine held, nine out.

"You sweep like someone who has never swept before." Shen Rui paused. "Who are you really, servant Wei?"

By morning, word had spread through the servants'' quarter: an elder was asking about the new girl.', 'published', now() - interval '88.131 days', now() - interval '88.131 days'),
  ('5f0c66b4-73bf-5e10-a57e-fa5f836cd402', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 6, 'The First Gate', 'In which Wei Lan opens the first of the Ninefold Path''s nine gates. Her damaged meridians begin to knit, painfully, along lines no sect manual describes.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

Her meridians ached as if packed with sand, and still the qi crept through them, slow and stubborn as a root through rock.

"Talent is common." Patriarch Gu paused. "Obedience is rare. This sect rewards the rare."

In the servants'' quarter, the kitchen fires smoked and the floor was always damp no matter how often it was swept.

Every face in the inner sect might have been there that night. She had to learn which ones.

"In this sect, the ones who bow lowest often climb highest. Remember that," Shen Rui said.

By morning, word had spread through the servants'' quarter: an elder was asking about the new girl.', 'published', now() - interval '85.380 days', now() - interval '85.380 days'),
  ('04bc4de5-b09e-5c61-ab9f-0aaa4d599f4c', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 7, 'Outer Sect Trials', 'In which servants may enter the outer sect by passing the annual trials. Wei Lan enters under a false name, Lan Shi, to avoid her family name being recognised.

Mist clung to the nine peaks of the Azure Summit, and the bells of the inner sect drifted down through it like falling leaves.

The jade slip grew a little warmer each time she followed its method. She chose not to wonder why.

Elder Mo said, "The Dao does not care how much you hate. It cares how long you can sit still."

Pine resin and incense hung in the air of the Scripture Pavilion, along with the dust of a thousand unread scrolls.

Her meridians ached as if packed with sand, and still the qi crept through them, slow and stubborn as a root through rock.

"Talent is common. Obedience is rare. This sect rewards the rare," Patriarch Gu said.

Far above, the Patriarch opened his eyes for the first time in a decade of seclusion.', 'published', now() - interval '83.150 days', now() - interval '83.150 days'),
  ('d3ee70fd-5ca1-5d6e-a24b-124956e11841', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 8, 'Stone Bridge', 'In which The first trial is crossing a bridge of shifting stones. Wei Lan crosses by feeling the qi in each stone rather than watching them.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

She reminded herself that a servant who looks up is noticed, and a servant who is noticed does not survive.

"Revenge is a fire." Elder Mo paused. "Keep it small enough to warm your hands, not large enough to burn your house."

