  ('cb316a2f-e367-5577-a245-89bab655473c', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 38, 'Recognition', 'In which Wei Lan names herself before the sect: Wei Lan, last of the Wei family. Patriarch Gu smiles, and the mountain begins to tremble.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

She reminded herself that a servant who looks up is noticed, and a servant who is noticed does not survive.

"Revenge is a fire. Keep it small enough to warm your hands, not large enough to burn your house," Elder Mo said.

In the servants'' quarter, the kitchen fires smoked and the floor was always damp no matter how often it was swept.

The jade slip grew a little warmer each time she followed its method. She chose not to wonder why.

Elder Mo said, "The Dao does not care how much you hate. It cares how long you can sit still."

Far above, the Patriarch opened his eyes for the first time in a decade of seclusion.', 'published', now() - interval '6.769 days', now() - interval '6.769 days'),
  ('43f43bb0-fce2-5db0-a632-64fb1901d0b8', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 39, 'The Patriarch Descends', 'In which Gu attacks to seize her method. Elder Mo, Shen Rui and, unexpectedly, half the servants of the sect step into his way.

Mist clung to the nine peaks of the Azure Summit, and the bells of the inner sect drifted down through it like falling leaves.

Wei Lan counted her breaths the way her grandfather had taught her: nine in, nine held, nine out.

Shen Rui said, "You sweep like someone who has never swept before. Who are you really, servant Wei?"

Pine resin and incense hung in the air of the Scripture Pavilion, along with the dust of a thousand unread scrolls.

She reminded herself that a servant who looks up is noticed, and a servant who is noticed does not survive.

"Revenge is a fire." Elder Mo paused. "Keep it small enough to warm your hands, not large enough to burn your house."

Far above, the Patriarch opened his eyes for the first time in a decade of seclusion.', 'published', now() - interval '4.563 days', now() - interval '4.563 days'),
  ('ab041328-294a-55dc-a3d0-4716fbb844ca', 'e52b45b3-2a54-56cf-acb1-0637ace80fa8', 40, 'What a Thousand Bows Are Worth', 'In which The servants Wei Lan once swept beside block the arena gates with their bodies. Gu hesitates, and the whole sect sees him hesitate.

The training grounds rang with the clash of wooden swords and the shouts of outer disciples counting forms.

Every face in the inner sect might have been there that night. She had to learn which ones.

"In this sect, the ones who bow lowest often climb highest. Remember that," Shen Rui said.

In the servants'' quarter, the kitchen fires smoked and the floor was always damp no matter how often it was swept.

Wei Lan counted her breaths the way her grandfather had taught her: nine in, nine held, nine out.

"You sweep like someone who has never swept before. Who are you really, servant Wei?" Shen Rui said.

When she returned to her mat, someone had searched her belongings and left everything exactly in place, except one thing.', 'published', now() - interval '1.861 days', now() - interval '1.861 days')
