Tess told herself it was an old house in an odd village and nothing more, and the house listened to her say it.

Mrs Pell said, "Your aunt was a good woman. She did what was asked. You''ll be asked too, dear."

Fog came off the water at dusk and crept up the garden as far as the kitchen step, and no further.

Every answer in this place arrived with a smile, and every smile seemed to close a door behind it.

