insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('b33cfd95-e979-5e23-aa90-98b77f115b81', '889c7e53-53ba-5022-a566-f39b3dc8b12c', 1, 'Beneath the Skylight', 'The body of Hasan Bey lay beneath the great skylight of the Silk Exchange, in a pool of morning sun so bright it seemed indecent.

Leyla Safi had been summoned for the ledgers, not the body, and she kept her eyes on the books as the inspector had asked. They were bound in red leather and written in Ottoman, Greek, French and a little Armenian, as merchants wrote when they did business with everyone and trusted no one.

On the first page, in Hasan Bey''s neat merchant hand, was a line that did not belong in any ledger. It was in Arabic, and it was addressed to a translator. ''If you are reading this,'' it said, ''they have already killed me. Read slowly.''

The call to prayer rose over Smyrna''s rooftops and tangled with church bells and the shouts of the harbour porters.

"In this city, Madame Safi, a locked door only means the key is in someone else''s pocket," Inspector Demir said.

Pressed between two pages was a strand of silk, dyed a red no merchant in Smyrna would admit to selling.', 'published', now() - interval '149.860 days', now() - interval '149.860 days'),
  ('d0c74532-1021-5ac7-aa14-85ba9030243b', '889c7e53-53ba-5022-a566-f39b3dc8b12c', 2, 'Five Languages', 'In which Leyla begins translating the ledgers. Hasan Bey switches languages mid-sentence, and the switches spell out a list of initials.

Evening light turned the bay to copper, and the steamers at anchor sent long smudges of smoke across the sky.

Each page she turned felt like a door opening onto a room someone had just left.

Inspector Demir said, "In this city, Madame Safi, a locked door only means the key is in someone else''s pocket."

Bales of silk stood stacked to the rafters of the Exchange, and the air smelled of dye, dust and lamp oil.

A ledger was a confession with the feelings taken out. She only had to put them back in.

Madame Vasse said, "Silk remembers every hand that touched it. People are less reliable."

When she reached home that evening, her study door was unlocked, and she had locked it.', 'published', now() - interval '145.198 days', now() - interval '145.198 days'),
  ('aaa6b983-5ee3-585c-ad5c-9a79a2f4eaf2', '889c7e53-53ba-5022-a566-f39b3dc8b12c', 3, 'Inspector Demir', 'In which Inspector Demir wants a quick verdict blaming a thief. He allows Leyla to keep working only because no one else can read the books.

The call to prayer rose over Smyrna''s rooftops and tangled with church bells and the shouts of the harbour porters.

In Smyrna a woman translator was useful, which was not the same as safe.

Inspector Demir said, "Translate what is written. Leave what it means to the police."

Rain hammered the cobbles of the Frankish quarter, and every doorway sheltered someone pretending not to listen.

Each page she turned felt like a door opening onto a room someone had just left.

Inspector Demir said, "In this city, Madame Safi, a locked door only means the key is in someone else''s pocket."

When she reached home that evening, her study door was unlocked, and she had locked it.', 'published', now() - interval '140.744 days', now() - interval '140.744 days'),
