Evening light turned the bay to copper, and the steamers at anchor sent long smudges of smoke across the sky.

Leyla had always believed every language had a word for the truth. She was learning that some of them had several.

"Every merchant here owes every other merchant. A murder is just a debt paid early," Aris said.

Bales of silk stood stacked to the rafters of the Exchange, and the air smelled of dye, dust and lamp oil.

In Smyrna a woman translator was useful, which was not the same as safe.

"Translate what is written." Inspector Demir paused. "Leave what it means to the police."

