insert into public.chapters (id, story_id, number, title, body, status, published_at, created_at) values
  ('c1e5c8c0-5543-5d2b-a33b-931e8774eee9', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 1, 'Cell F112', 'The last thing Kenji Mori saw on Earth was cell F112 of a quarterly reconciliation, which did not balance.

The first thing he saw in his new life was a glowing crystal the size of a refrigerator, which said, in a voice like a sleepy bell: ''Oh good. You''re the accountant.''

Kenji looked down. He was wearing a robe, sitting in a chair carved from what seemed to be a giant mushroom, and holding a quill. In front of him on a stone desk lay a single scroll titled FOURTH LABYRINTH: EXPENSES (APPROXIMATE).

''Approximate,'' Kenji said faintly.

''We''ve been very busy,'' said the crystal.

Torches lined the corridors of the Fourth Labyrinth, and most of them were, Kenji noted, burning money.

"We used to have a budget. Then we had a dragon. It was a difficult year," Core said.

The next ledger he opened was written in blood, which seemed unnecessarily dramatic for a stationery order.', 'published', now() - interval '65.689 days', now() - interval '65.689 days'),
  ('132f6669-90fd-50d1-a88b-4bce75302bfb', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 2, 'Expenses (Approximate)', 'In which Kenji reads the dungeon''s finances: three hundred years of unpaid bills, an absurd torch budget, and a dragon who buys gold with borrowed gold.

Slimes bounced through the staff corridor in the morning rush, each carrying a tiny lunch.

Kenji realised that, for the first time in his life, the people he was working for actually said thank you.

"We used to have a budget. Then we had a dragon. It was a difficult year," Core said.

Somewhere in the lower floors a trap clanked, reset itself, and clanked again for no one in particular.

Every line item in the Fourth Labyrinth told a story, and most of the stories were about a dragon buying things.

Pip slid under the office door with a letter bearing the Guild''s seal, and it was not good news.', 'published', now() - interval '63.600 days', now() - interval '63.600 days'),
  ('f68fac0f-dabf-571a-aca7-d9925a45ee18', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 3, 'One Month', 'In which the Core reveals the Adventurers'' Guild holds the dungeon''s debt and will seize it in one month to turn it into a theme park.

Torches lined the corridors of the Fourth Labyrinth, and most of them were, Kenji noted, burning money.

There was a strange pleasure in finding a missing number. It was the same in any world.

"Please do not use the word ''audit'' near the ninth floor. It upsets the dragon," Core said.

The dragon''s lair on the ninth floor smelled of old gold, smoke and, faintly, chamomile tea.

Kenji realised that, for the first time in his life, the people he was working for actually said thank you.

"We used to have a budget. Then we had a dragon. It was a difficult year," Core said.

From the ninth floor came the sound of a very large creature crying quietly into a pile of coins.', 'published', now() - interval '61.318 days', now() - interval '61.318 days'),
  ('c8d1ed8b-0ef8-5a08-a97f-117d5ac6649c', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 4, 'Pip', 'In which Kenji meets Pip, a cheerful slime who becomes his assistant mainly because he can fit under locked doors to fetch records.

Slimes bounced through the staff corridor in the morning rush, each carrying a tiny lunch.

Kenji had died of overwork. He was beginning to suspect he had been reincarnated for more of it.

"I have hoarded gold for four centuries and I still don''t know what interest is," Ignatia said.

Somewhere in the lower floors a trap clanked, reset itself, and clanked again for no one in particular.

There was a strange pleasure in finding a missing number. It was the same in any world.

"Please do not use the word ''audit'' near the ninth floor. It upsets the dragon," Core said.

Pip slid under the office door with a letter bearing the Guild''s seal, and it was not good news.', 'published', now() - interval '59.137 days', now() - interval '59.137 days'),
  ('c4e9ac73-785d-5b39-ad43-a39a60b10409', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 5, 'The Slime Union', 'In which the slimes complain they have never been paid. Kenji discovers their wages have been ''reinvested'' into the dragon''s hoard for two centuries.

Torches lined the corridors of the Fourth Labyrinth, and most of them were, Kenji noted, burning money.

He kept meaning to be horrified about being dead. There was always another invoice first.

Ignatia said, "If you make me fill out one more form, accountant, I will be very politely on fire."

The dragon''s lair on the ninth floor smelled of old gold, smoke and, faintly, chamomile tea.

Kenji had died of overwork. He was beginning to suspect he had been reincarnated for more of it.

Ignatia said, "I have hoarded gold for four centuries and I still don''t know what interest is."

The Core flickered, and a new number appeared in the debts column. It was much larger than the old one.', 'published', now() - interval '56.972 days', now() - interval '56.972 days'),
