  ('3d2ca04f-cc2c-5f8b-aa73-bd35d52225fd', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 28, 'Celebration', 'In which the dungeon throws its first staff party in three centuries. Ignatia lights the bonfire and only sets a little of the ceiling on fire.

Slimes bounced through the staff corridor in the morning rush, each carrying a tiny lunch.

There was a strange pleasure in finding a missing number. It was the same in any world.

Core said, "Please do not use the word ''audit'' near the ninth floor. It upsets the dragon."

Somewhere in the lower floors a trap clanked, reset itself, and clanked again for no one in particular.

Kenji realised that, for the first time in his life, the people he was working for actually said thank you.

"We used to have a budget. Then we had a dragon. It was a difficult year," Core said.

A Guild inspector had been seen at the dungeon entrance, taking notes.', 'published', now() - interval '5.754 days', now() - interval '5.754 days'),
  ('6538cfef-8917-5a21-a74b-7e5fc4c20265', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 29, 'Year-End Close', 'In which Kenji closes the Fourth Labyrinth''s books for the year. For the first time in either of his lives, everything balances.

Torches lined the corridors of the Fourth Labyrinth, and most of them were, Kenji noted, burning money.

Kenji had died of overwork. He was beginning to suspect he had been reincarnated for more of it.

Ignatia said, "I have hoarded gold for four centuries and I still don''t know what interest is."

The dragon''s lair on the ninth floor smelled of old gold, smoke and, faintly, chamomile tea.

There was a strange pleasure in finding a missing number. It was the same in any world.

Core said, "Please do not use the word ''audit'' near the ninth floor. It upsets the dragon."

The Core flickered, and a new number appeared in the debts column. It was much larger than the old one.', 'published', now() - interval '3.835 days', now() - interval '3.835 days'),
  ('ff6de55c-1bdf-50fc-abfd-60d64a952d09', '7cd412ed-2a47-53de-a984-e67d223c5649', 30, 'A New Ledger', 'In which a letter arrives from a distant, failing dungeon asking for help. Kenji looks at the Core, picks up his quill, and opens a new ledger.

Slimes bounced through the staff corridor in the morning rush, each carrying a tiny lunch.

He kept meaning to be horrified about being dead. There was always another invoice first.

"If you make me fill out one more form, accountant, I will be very politely on fire," Ignatia said quietly.

Somewhere in the lower floors a trap clanked, reset itself, and clanked again for no one in particular.

Kenji had died of overwork. He was beginning to suspect he had been reincarnated for more of it.

A Guild inspector had been seen at the dungeon entrance, taking notes.', 'published', now() - interval '1.500 days', now() - interval '1.500 days')
